@module flutter-m12 | Animations
@summary Bring UIs to life with implicit and explicit animations, Hero, transitions, Rive and Lottie.

@lesson flutter-m12-l01 | Implicit animations | 8
## Learning objectives
- Animate by changing properties

## Implicit animations
Implicitly animated widgets (`AnimatedOpacity`, `AnimatedContainer`, `AnimatedPadding`...) animate automatically when their properties change.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget fade(bool visible) => AnimatedOpacity(
      opacity: visible ? 1 : 0,
      duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 300),
      child: const Text('Hello'),
    );
```

## Summary
- Change a value, Flutter animates it.

@lesson flutter-m12-l02 | Explicit animations | 8
## Learning objectives
- Control animations precisely

## Explicit animations
Explicit animations use an `AnimationController` you start, stop, repeat or reverse. Use them for looping or interactive animations.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

class Pulse extends StatefulWidget {
  const Pulse({super.key});
  @override
  State<Pulse> createState() => _PulseState();
}

class _PulseState extends State<Pulse> with SingleTickerProviderStateMixin {
  late final _c = AnimationController(vsync: this, duration: const Duration(seconds: 1))..repeat(reverse: true);
  @override
  void dispose() { _c.dispose(); super.dispose(); }
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => ScaleTransition(scale: Tween(begin: 0.9, end: 1.1).animate(_c), child: const Icon(Icons.favorite));
}
```

## Summary
- Explicit = you own the controller.

@lesson flutter-m12-l03 | AnimationController | 8
## Learning objectives
- Drive animations over time

## AnimationController
AnimationController produces values 0.0→1.0 synced to the screen refresh via a `TickerProvider`. Always dispose it.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

// inside a State with SingleTickerProviderStateMixin:
// late final controller = AnimationController(vsync: this, duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 500));
// controller.forward(); controller.reverse();
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Needs vsync and dispose.

@lesson flutter-m12-l04 | Tween | 8
## Learning objectives
- Map 0–1 to any range

## Tween
A `Tween` maps the controller's progress to colours, sizes or offsets; `CurvedAnimation` adds easing.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Animation<double> grow(AnimationController c) =>
    Tween<double>(begin: 0, end: 200).animate(CurvedAnimation(parent: c, curve: Curves.easeOutBack));
```

## Summary
- Tweens map progress to values.

@lesson flutter-m12-l05 | Hero animations | 8
## Learning objectives
- Fly widgets between screens

## Hero animations
Wrap matching widgets on two routes in `Hero` with the same tag; Flutter animates between them during navigation.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget thumb(String id) => Hero(tag: 'img-$id', child: const Icon(Icons.image, size: 48));
```

## Summary
- Tags must match and be unique per screen.

@lesson flutter-m12-l06 | AnimatedContainer | 8
## Learning objectives
- Animate size, colour and shape together

## AnimatedContainer
AnimatedContainer animates any changed Container property.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget box(bool selected) => AnimatedContainer(
      duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 250),
      width: selected ? 120 : 80,
      height: 80,
      decoration: BoxDecoration(color: selected ? Colors.indigo : Colors.grey, borderRadius: BorderRadius.circular(selected ? 24 : 8)),
    );
```

## Summary
- Great for selection states.

@lesson flutter-m12-l07 | AnimatedSwitcher | 8
## Learning objectives
- Animate between different widgets

## AnimatedSwitcher
AnimatedSwitcher cross-fades (or custom-transitions) when its child changes. Give children different keys.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget counter(int n) => AnimatedSwitcher(
      duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 300),
      child: Text('$n', key: ValueKey(n)),
    );
```

## Summary
- Different keys trigger the switch.

@lesson flutter-m12-l08 | AnimatedBuilder | 8
## Learning objectives
- Rebuild only the animated part

## AnimatedBuilder
AnimatedBuilder listens to an animation and rebuilds only its builder, passing a pre-built child for efficiency.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget spin(Animation<double> a) => AnimatedBuilder(
      animation: a,
      child: const Icon(Icons.refresh),
      builder: (_, child) => Transform.rotate(angle: a.value * 6.28, child: child),
    );
```

## Summary
- Pass static subtrees as child.

@lesson flutter-m12-l09 | Custom transitions | 8
## Learning objectives
- Customise page transitions

## Custom transitions
`PageRouteBuilder` lets you define custom route transitions such as fade or slide.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Route<void> fadeRoute(Widget page) => PageRouteBuilder(
      pageBuilder: (_, __, ___) => page,
      transitionsBuilder: (_, animation, __, child) => FadeTransition(opacity: animation, child: child),
    );
```

## Summary
- PageRouteBuilder customises transitions.

@lesson flutter-m12-l10 | Rive integration | 8
## Learning objectives
- Use interactive vector animations

## Rive integration
Rive animations are designed in the Rive editor and support state machines that react to input. Add the `rive` package and load a `.riv` asset.

```dart
// RiveAnimation.asset('assets/bimo.riv', stateMachines: const ['Main'])
void main() {}
```

## Summary
- Rive suits interactive, stateful animations.

@lesson flutter-m12-l11 | Lottie integration | 8
## Learning objectives
- Play After Effects animations

## Lottie integration
Lottie plays JSON animations exported from After Effects. Great for empty states and celebrations.

```dart
import 'package:lottie/lottie.dart';
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

Widget celebrate() => Lottie.asset('assets/confetti.json', repeat: false, width: 200);
```

## Summary
- Use Lottie for designer-made animations.
